<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE HermitCrabInput SYSTEM "HermitCrabInput.dtd">
<!-- Morphotactic attribute breadth. Closes the coverage-ledger entries that need no phonological
     feature system: repetition caps, partial rules/entries, bound allomorphs, non-final templates,
     co-occurrence rules, and MPR feature groups. Stratum cyclicity and phonologicalRuleOrder are
     declared below (Main) purely for the enumerated value's presence in a document: grep the whole
     of src/SIL.Machine.Morphology.HermitCrab for "Cyclicity"/"PhonologicalRuleOrder" and Stratum.cs's
     own property list, and neither exists anywhere outside the DTD and XmlLanguageLoader's unread
     Stratum attribute text; the loader never even reads them into a discarded local, let alone acts
     on them. No fixture can make either surface observable; that is a product gap, not a modeling gap.

     Converted to fieldworks_producible: true (see words.yaml history note for the prior state and
     what did not survive). Two independent, previously unrecorded findings drove the biggest changes
     here, beyond the four causes the prior notes already named:

     - HCLoader.cs never sets LexicalEntry.Family (grep confirmed zero hits) and never touches
       Blockable on any rule (grep confirmed zero hits for "Blockable" in HCLoader.cs), so the
       entire family/blockable/Word.CheckBlocking mechanism is unreachable from a FieldWorks project,
       not merely the specific "family-blocking" label the prior notes used. Every construct here
       that depended on it (the MorphologicalRule@blockable="false" probe, the RealizationalRule@
       blockable="false" probe, both suppletive-sibling families) is gone, not converted: no
       FieldWorks-producible substitute exists for CheckBlocking itself (see
       conformance/docs/engine-only-fixture-retirement.md).
     - Main's own morphologicalRuleOrder="linear" mattered to this fixture's ground truth (the
       conferExcl/exclReader exclusion pair is legible only because one order is tried), so
       PROTOCOL.md section 9's fourth usage-level check applied: MorphologicalRuleOrder must not
       matter to a fixture's committed ground truth; HCLoader hardcodes every Stratum to Unordered
       and can never emit linear. Switched to "unordered" and every word re-verified against the C#
       founding oracle under that order; see words.yaml for what changed and what did not.

     Repetition is the reason this fixture exists at all. multipleApplication has NO effect on a rule
     reached through an AffixTemplate slot, because a template applies each slot once (established
     against the C# oracle in edge-cases/loader-isactive-breadth). Every repeatable rule here is
     therefore listed on the Stratum's own morphologicalRules attribute instead, where the cap is
     observable: mrRep0 must never apply, and mrRep2 must apply at most twice. Those two boundaries
     are what the ledger's remaining multipleApplication values are quotiented against.

     MorphologicalRule@partial gets its OWN unordered Second stratum below: partial only gates a
     rule NOT reachable through any Slot (SynthesisAffixProcessRule.cs's IsTemplateRule check), and a
     template-then-stratum-rule ordering only exists via the Unordered ApplyTemplates-then-
     ApplyMorphologicalRules recursion in SynthesisStratumRule.cs.

     Every decoy carries isActive="no" and is named by the word whose outcome observes it, per
     words.yaml's neutralizes: lists. -->
<HermitCrabInput>
  <Language>
    <Name>MorphotacticAttributeBreadth</Name>
    <PartsOfSpeech>
      <PartOfSpeech id="posN"><Name>n</Name></PartOfSpeech>
    </PartsOfSpeech>
    <MorphologicalPhonologicalRuleFeatures>
      <MorphologicalPhonologicalRuleFeature id="mprA">A</MorphologicalPhonologicalRuleFeature>
      <MorphologicalPhonologicalRuleFeature id="mprB">B</MorphologicalPhonologicalRuleFeature>
      <!-- Bucket-2 coverage (MorphologicalOutput.MPRFeatures -> MorphologicalInput.excludedMPRFeatures):
           an affix confers a flag that blocks a LATER affix. HCLoader.cs:969 (AffixProcessAllomorph.
           OutMprFeatures) writes the payload, HCLoader.cs:1717 (AffixProcessAllomorph.
           ExcludedMprFeatures) reads it. Ungrouped deliberately: this is a direct exclusion, not an
           overwrite-group interaction (see mrGrpSetA/mrGrpSetB/mrGrpReq below). -->
      <MorphologicalPhonologicalRuleFeature id="mprExclFlag">ExclFlag</MorphologicalPhonologicalRuleFeature>
      <!-- FieldWorks-producible replacement for the prior appendGroup/groupDecoy pair: HCLoader.cs
           (LoadLanguage, :168-192) only ever builds THREE hardcoded, always-Overwrite groups:
           "inflClasses" (matchType Any), "exceptionFeatures" (matchType All), "lexEntryInflTypes"
           (matchType All); never a user-named group, and never a group whose Output is anything but
           the engine default (Overwrite). No existing fixture (staged or upstream, checked via
           grep across every grammar.xml) exercises any of the three real names, so naming this group
           "exceptionFeatures" with the matching matchType="all" and the default (omitted, i.e.
           Overwrite) outputType is new, not duplicate, coverage of a real HCLoader-producible
           surface: MorphologicalPhonologicalRuleFeatureGroup.features is "Yes" in
           fieldworks-producibility.tsv but had no witnessing fixture before this one. What is lost:
           outputType="append" itself. HCLoader never sets Output away from Overwrite, so append
           semantics have no FieldWorks-producible fixture anywhere in this suite; see
           conformance/docs/engine-only-fixture-retirement.md for where that construct's own coverage
           now lives (mpr-group-overwrite-without-realizational / mpr-overwrite-order-dependence,
           both still engine-only). -->
      <MorphologicalPhonologicalRuleFeatureGroup matchType="all" features="mprA mprB">
        <Name>exceptionFeatures</Name>
      </MorphologicalPhonologicalRuleFeatureGroup>
    </MorphologicalPhonologicalRuleFeatures>
    <CharacterDefinitionTable id="tbl">
      <Name>Main</Name>
      <SegmentDefinitions>
        <SegmentDefinition id="sA"><Representations><Representation>a</Representation></Representations></SegmentDefinition>
        <SegmentDefinition id="sE"><Representations><Representation>e</Representation></Representations></SegmentDefinition>
        <SegmentDefinition id="sI"><Representations><Representation>i</Representation></Representations></SegmentDefinition>
        <SegmentDefinition id="sO"><Representations><Representation>o</Representation></Representations></SegmentDefinition>
        <SegmentDefinition id="sU"><Representations><Representation>u</Representation></Representations></SegmentDefinition>
        <SegmentDefinition id="sB"><Representations><Representation>b</Representation></Representations></SegmentDefinition>
        <SegmentDefinition id="sD"><Representations><Representation>d</Representation></Representations></SegmentDefinition>
        <SegmentDefinition id="sG"><Representations><Representation>g</Representation></Representations></SegmentDefinition>
        <SegmentDefinition id="sK"><Representations><Representation>k</Representation></Representations></SegmentDefinition>
        <SegmentDefinition id="sL"><Representations><Representation>l</Representation></Representations></SegmentDefinition>
        <SegmentDefinition id="sM"><Representations><Representation>m</Representation></Representations></SegmentDefinition>
        <SegmentDefinition id="sN"><Representations><Representation>n</Representation></Representations></SegmentDefinition>
        <SegmentDefinition id="sP"><Representations><Representation>p</Representation></Representations></SegmentDefinition>
        <SegmentDefinition id="sR"><Representations><Representation>r</Representation></Representations></SegmentDefinition>
        <SegmentDefinition id="sS"><Representations><Representation>s</Representation></Representations></SegmentDefinition>
        <SegmentDefinition id="sT"><Representations><Representation>t</Representation></Representations></SegmentDefinition>
      </SegmentDefinitions>
    </CharacterDefinitionTable>
    <NaturalClasses>
      <FeatureNaturalClass id="ncAny"><Name>Any</Name></FeatureNaturalClass>
    </NaturalClasses>
    <Strata>
      <!-- cyclicity="cyclic" and phonologicalRuleOrder="simultaneous" are both non-default. This
           stratum declares no phonological rules, so the rule-order value is a load-time property
           here rather than an observable ordering; the ledger records it accordingly. Neither
           attribute has a producibility question of its own: Stratum.cs carries no corresponding
           engine property at all (see the file header), so HCLoader has no path to write either
           value regardless; the DTD default and any explicit value are equally unreachable from a
           real project, and equally inert in the engine. morphologicalRuleOrder="unordered" (below)
           is the one Stratum attribute that IS engine-real and IS HCLoader-producible (HCLoader
           hardcodes Unordered on every Stratum it builds; see the file header for why this fixture
           had to move off "linear" to convert). -->
      <Stratum characterDefinitionTable="tbl" morphologicalRuleOrder="unordered" cyclicity="cyclic"
               phonologicalRuleOrder="simultaneous"
               morphologicalRules="mrRep0 mrRep2 mrConferExcl mrGrpSetB mrGrpSetA mrGrpReq"
               isActive="yes">
        <Name>Main</Name>
        <MorphologicalRuleDefinitions>
          <!-- multipleApplication="0": the cap is zero, so this suffix must never attach. -->
          <MorphologicalRule id="mrRep0" multipleApplication="0" requiredPartsOfSpeech="posN" outputPartOfSpeech="posN">
            <Name>neverApplies</Name>
            <MorphologicalSubrules>
              <MorphologicalSubrule id="subRep0">
                <MorphologicalInput><PhoneticSequence id="stem0"><OptionalSegmentSequence min="1" max="-1"><SimpleContext naturalClass="ncAny" /></OptionalSegmentSequence></PhoneticSequence></MorphologicalInput>
                <MorphologicalOutput><CopyFromInput index="stem0" /><InsertSegments><PhoneticShape>ba</PhoneticShape></InsertSegments></MorphologicalOutput>
              </MorphologicalSubrule>
            </MorphologicalSubrules>
            <MorphemeId>NEVER</MorphemeId>
            <Gloss>never</Gloss>
          </MorphologicalRule>
          <!-- multipleApplication="2": at most two copies of this suffix. -->
          <MorphologicalRule id="mrRep2" multipleApplication="2" requiredPartsOfSpeech="posN" outputPartOfSpeech="posN">
            <Name>twiceAtMost</Name>
            <MorphologicalSubrules>
              <MorphologicalSubrule id="subRep2">
                <MorphologicalInput><PhoneticSequence id="stem2"><OptionalSegmentSequence min="1" max="-1"><SimpleContext naturalClass="ncAny" /></OptionalSegmentSequence></PhoneticSequence></MorphologicalInput>
                <MorphologicalOutput><CopyFromInput index="stem2" /><InsertSegments><PhoneticShape>de</PhoneticShape></InsertSegments></MorphologicalOutput>
              </MorphologicalSubrule>
            </MorphologicalSubrules>
            <MorphemeId>TWICE</MorphemeId>
            <Gloss>twice</Gloss>
          </MorphologicalRule>
          <MorphologicalRule id="mrNF" requiredPartsOfSpeech="posN" outputPartOfSpeech="posN">
            <Name>nfOnly</Name>
            <MorphologicalSubrules>
              <MorphologicalSubrule id="subNF">
                <MorphologicalInput><PhoneticSequence id="stemNF"><OptionalSegmentSequence min="1" max="-1"><SimpleContext naturalClass="ncAny" /></OptionalSegmentSequence></PhoneticSequence></MorphologicalInput>
                <MorphologicalOutput><CopyFromInput index="stemNF" /><InsertSegments><PhoneticShape>pu</PhoneticShape></InsertSegments></MorphologicalOutput>
              </MorphologicalSubrule>
            </MorphologicalSubrules>
            <MorphemeId>NF</MorphemeId>
            <Gloss>nf</Gloss>
          </MorphologicalRule>
          <!-- partial="true": a partially specified rule. -->
          <MorphologicalRule id="mrPartial" partial="true" requiredPartsOfSpeech="posN" outputPartOfSpeech="posN">
            <Name>partialRule</Name>
            <MorphologicalSubrules>
              <MorphologicalSubrule id="subPartial">
                <MorphologicalInput><PhoneticSequence id="stemP"><OptionalSegmentSequence min="1" max="-1"><SimpleContext naturalClass="ncAny" /></OptionalSegmentSequence></PhoneticSequence></MorphologicalInput>
                <MorphologicalOutput><CopyFromInput index="stemP" /><InsertSegments><PhoneticShape>mo</PhoneticShape></InsertSegments></MorphologicalOutput>
              </MorphologicalSubrule>
            </MorphologicalSubrules>
            <MorphemeId>PART</MorphemeId>
            <Gloss>part</Gloss>
          </MorphologicalRule>
          <!-- mrCoA/mrCoB/mrCoC/mrCoD: four isolated ordinary suffixes, kept from the pre-conversion
               grammar purely for affix-stacking and Slot-ordering coverage (topsakatana,
               topsakanabu below) now that no co-occurrence rule references them; see mrExA/mrExB
               below for where AllomorphCoOccurrenceRule/MorphemeCoOccurrenceRule coverage now lives. -->
          <MorphologicalRule id="mrCoA" requiredPartsOfSpeech="posN" outputPartOfSpeech="posN">
            <Name>coA</Name>
            <MorphologicalSubrules>
              <MorphologicalSubrule id="subCoA">
                <MorphologicalInput><PhoneticSequence id="stemCoA"><OptionalSegmentSequence min="1" max="-1"><SimpleContext naturalClass="ncAny" /></OptionalSegmentSequence></PhoneticSequence></MorphologicalInput>
                <MorphologicalOutput><CopyFromInput index="stemCoA" /><InsertSegments><PhoneticShape>sa</PhoneticShape></InsertSegments></MorphologicalOutput>
              </MorphologicalSubrule>
            </MorphologicalSubrules>
            <MorphemeId>COA</MorphemeId>
            <Gloss>coa</Gloss>
          </MorphologicalRule>
          <MorphologicalRule id="mrCoB" requiredPartsOfSpeech="posN" outputPartOfSpeech="posN">
            <Name>coB</Name>
            <MorphologicalSubrules>
              <MorphologicalSubrule id="subCoB">
                <MorphologicalInput><PhoneticSequence id="stemCoB"><OptionalSegmentSequence min="1" max="-1"><SimpleContext naturalClass="ncAny" /></OptionalSegmentSequence></PhoneticSequence></MorphologicalInput>
                <MorphologicalOutput><CopyFromInput index="stemCoB" /><InsertSegments><PhoneticShape>ka</PhoneticShape></InsertSegments></MorphologicalOutput>
              </MorphologicalSubrule>
            </MorphologicalSubrules>
            <MorphemeId>COB</MorphemeId>
            <Gloss>cob</Gloss>
          </MorphologicalRule>
          <MorphologicalRule id="mrCoC" requiredPartsOfSpeech="posN" outputPartOfSpeech="posN">
            <Name>coC</Name>
            <MorphologicalSubrules>
              <MorphologicalSubrule id="subCoC">
                <MorphologicalInput><PhoneticSequence id="stemCoC"><OptionalSegmentSequence min="1" max="-1"><SimpleContext naturalClass="ncAny" /></OptionalSegmentSequence></PhoneticSequence></MorphologicalInput>
                <MorphologicalOutput><CopyFromInput index="stemCoC" /><InsertSegments><PhoneticShape>ta</PhoneticShape></InsertSegments></MorphologicalOutput>
              </MorphologicalSubrule>
            </MorphologicalSubrules>
            <MorphemeId>COC</MorphemeId>
            <Gloss>coc</Gloss>
          </MorphologicalRule>
          <MorphologicalRule id="mrCoD" requiredPartsOfSpeech="posN" outputPartOfSpeech="posN">
            <Name>coD</Name>
            <MorphologicalSubrules>
              <MorphologicalSubrule id="subCoD">
                <MorphologicalInput><PhoneticSequence id="stemCoD"><OptionalSegmentSequence min="1" max="-1"><SimpleContext naturalClass="ncAny" /></OptionalSegmentSequence></PhoneticSequence></MorphologicalInput>
                <MorphologicalOutput><CopyFromInput index="stemCoD" /><InsertSegments><PhoneticShape>na</PhoneticShape></InsertSegments></MorphologicalOutput>
              </MorphologicalSubrule>
            </MorphologicalSubrules>
            <MorphemeId>COD</MorphemeId>
            <Gloss>cod</Gloss>
          </MorphologicalRule>
          <!-- mrMB: kept only for the topsakanabu Slot-ordering discriminator below (coDSlot~mbSlot).
               Its prior MorphologicalOutput.MPRFeatures="mprB" write is gone: a rule reached only
               through an AffixTemplate Slot is necessarily inflectional, and LoadInflAffixProcessRule
               never sets MPR features on an inflectional rule (PROTOCOL.md section 9), so that write
               could never come from FieldWorks regardless of which group it fed. The MPR-group
               read/write pair this rule used to help demonstrate now lives entirely on mrGrpSetA/
               mrGrpSetB/mrGrpReq below, which are stratum-level (never template-slot), where writing
               MPR features IS producible. -->
          <MorphologicalRule id="mrMB" requiredPartsOfSpeech="posN" outputPartOfSpeech="posN">
            <Name>setMB</Name>
            <MorphologicalSubrules>
              <MorphologicalSubrule id="subMB">
                <MorphologicalInput><PhoneticSequence id="stemMB"><OptionalSegmentSequence min="1" max="-1"><SimpleContext naturalClass="ncAny" /></OptionalSegmentSequence></PhoneticSequence></MorphologicalInput>
                <MorphologicalOutput><CopyFromInput index="stemMB" /><InsertSegments><PhoneticShape>bu</PhoneticShape></InsertSegments></MorphologicalOutput>
              </MorphologicalSubrule>
            </MorphologicalSubrules>
            <MorphemeId>MB</MorphemeId>
            <Gloss>mb</Gloss>
          </MorphologicalRule>
          <!-- Bucket-2 coverage: the affix-conferred-blocking pair. mrConferExcl's own
               MorphologicalOutput.MPRFeatures write (mprExclFlag) is the writer under test; applying
               it before mrExclReader means mrExclReader's own MorphologicalInput.excludedMPRFeatures
               gate blocks: a later affix refusing to attach once an earlier one has marked the stem,
               e.g. a derivational suffix that makes a further derivation ineligible.

               The writer (mrConferExcl) and reader (mrExclReader) have OPPOSITE location
               requirements, confirmed by fieldworks-producibility.tsv and by
               edge-cases/mpr-gated-exception's own words.yaml (the very fixture this task's family-
               blocking conversion is meant to follow the pattern of, and the reason IT stays
               fieldworks_producible: false overall): MorphologicalOutput.MPRFeatures is producible
               only on a rule reached OUTSIDE any AffixTemplate Slot (LoadInflAffixProcessRule never
               sets it on an inflectional/templated rule), while MorphologicalInput.excludedMPRFeatures
               is producible only on a rule reached THROUGH a Slot (HCLoader.cs:1717 is its sole
               assignment site, inside LoadAffixTemplate's own slot-blocking loop; a stratum-level
               rule's excludedMPRFeatures has no HCLoader path at all; see mpr-gated-exception's own
               mrSuf, which is exactly this shape and is the HC-engine-only half of that fixture). So
               mrConferExcl stays stratum-level here and mrExclReader moves into finalTemplate's own
               exclReaderSlot below: the only placement where BOTH halves of this bucket-2 pair are
               simultaneously producible. (The pre-conversion version of this fixture had both rules
               stratum-level, which means its own fieldworks_producible: false verdict, while correct
               in outcome, understated its causes: this specific shape was never named among them.) -->
          <MorphologicalRule id="mrConferExcl" requiredPartsOfSpeech="posN" outputPartOfSpeech="posN">
            <Name>conferExcl</Name>
            <MorphologicalSubrules>
              <MorphologicalSubrule id="subConferExcl">
                <MorphologicalInput><PhoneticSequence id="stemConferExcl"><OptionalSegmentSequence min="1" max="-1"><SimpleContext naturalClass="ncAny" /></OptionalSegmentSequence></PhoneticSequence></MorphologicalInput>
                <MorphologicalOutput MPRFeatures="mprExclFlag"><CopyFromInput index="stemConferExcl" /><InsertSegments><PhoneticShape>do</PhoneticShape></InsertSegments></MorphologicalOutput>
              </MorphologicalSubrule>
            </MorphologicalSubrules>
            <MorphemeId>CONFEREXCL</MorphemeId>
            <Gloss>conferexcl</Gloss>
          </MorphologicalRule>
          <MorphologicalRule id="mrExclReader" requiredPartsOfSpeech="posN" outputPartOfSpeech="posN">
            <Name>exclReader</Name>
            <MorphologicalSubrules>
              <MorphologicalSubrule id="subExclReader">
                <MorphologicalInput excludedMPRFeatures="mprExclFlag"><PhoneticSequence id="stemExclReader"><OptionalSegmentSequence min="1" max="-1"><SimpleContext naturalClass="ncAny" /></OptionalSegmentSequence></PhoneticSequence></MorphologicalInput>
                <MorphologicalOutput><CopyFromInput index="stemExclReader" /><InsertSegments><PhoneticShape>ri</PhoneticShape></InsertSegments></MorphologicalOutput>
              </MorphologicalSubrule>
            </MorphologicalSubrules>
            <MorphemeId>EXCLREADER</MorphemeId>
            <Gloss>exclreader</Gloss>
          </MorphologicalRule>
          <!-- MPR-group overwrite semantics (replaces the removed appendGroup/groupDecoy pair; see
               the MorphologicalPhonologicalRuleFeatureGroup comment above). All three rules are
               stratum-level, so their MPR-feature reads/writes are producible. mrGrpSetB confers
               mprB; mrGrpSetA confers mprA, and since both are members of "exceptionFeatures"
               (Overwrite, the only mode HCLoader ever produces), applying mrGrpSetA after mrGrpSetB
               evicts mprB group-wide; mrGrpReq then requires mprB still be present. -->
          <MorphologicalRule id="mrGrpSetB" requiredPartsOfSpeech="posN" outputPartOfSpeech="posN">
            <Name>grpSetB</Name>
            <MorphologicalSubrules>
              <MorphologicalSubrule id="subGrpSetB">
                <MorphologicalInput><PhoneticSequence id="stemGrpSetB"><OptionalSegmentSequence min="1" max="-1"><SimpleContext naturalClass="ncAny" /></OptionalSegmentSequence></PhoneticSequence></MorphologicalInput>
                <MorphologicalOutput MPRFeatures="mprB"><CopyFromInput index="stemGrpSetB" /><InsertSegments><PhoneticShape>ga</PhoneticShape></InsertSegments></MorphologicalOutput>
              </MorphologicalSubrule>
            </MorphologicalSubrules>
            <MorphemeId>GRPB</MorphemeId>
            <Gloss>grpb</Gloss>
          </MorphologicalRule>
          <MorphologicalRule id="mrGrpSetA" requiredPartsOfSpeech="posN" outputPartOfSpeech="posN">
            <Name>grpSetA</Name>
            <MorphologicalSubrules>
              <MorphologicalSubrule id="subGrpSetA">
                <MorphologicalInput><PhoneticSequence id="stemGrpSetA"><OptionalSegmentSequence min="1" max="-1"><SimpleContext naturalClass="ncAny" /></OptionalSegmentSequence></PhoneticSequence></MorphologicalInput>
                <MorphologicalOutput MPRFeatures="mprA"><CopyFromInput index="stemGrpSetA" /><InsertSegments><PhoneticShape>ge</PhoneticShape></InsertSegments></MorphologicalOutput>
              </MorphologicalSubrule>
            </MorphologicalSubrules>
            <MorphemeId>GRPA</MorphemeId>
            <Gloss>grpa</Gloss>
          </MorphologicalRule>
          <MorphologicalRule id="mrGrpReq" requiredPartsOfSpeech="posN" outputPartOfSpeech="posN">
            <Name>grpReq</Name>
            <MorphologicalSubrules>
              <MorphologicalSubrule id="subGrpReq">
                <MorphologicalInput requiredMPRFeatures="mprB"><PhoneticSequence id="stemGrpReq"><OptionalSegmentSequence min="1" max="-1"><SimpleContext naturalClass="ncAny" /></OptionalSegmentSequence></PhoneticSequence></MorphologicalInput>
                <MorphologicalOutput><CopyFromInput index="stemGrpReq" /><InsertSegments><PhoneticShape>go</PhoneticShape></InsertSegments></MorphologicalOutput>
              </MorphologicalSubrule>
            </MorphologicalSubrules>
            <MorphemeId>GRPREQ</MorphemeId>
            <Gloss>grpreq</Gloss>
          </MorphologicalRule>
          <!-- FieldWorks-producible replacement for the removed MorphemeCoOccurrenceRule/
               AllomorphCoOccurrenceRule type="require" pair (topsakatana's old four requires plus
               "sol"'s own require, all gone: HCLoader's two co-occurrence loaders build Exclude
               constraints only, sourced from prohibition-only LibLCM repositories, so type="require"
               has no FieldWorks equivalent at all, regardless of the surrounding rule). mrExA/mrExB
               are an isolated pair purely for this; see the AllomorphCoOccurrenceRules/
               MorphemeCoOccurrenceRules elements below. -->
          <MorphologicalRule id="mrExA" requiredPartsOfSpeech="posN" outputPartOfSpeech="posN">
            <Name>exA</Name>
            <MorphologicalSubrules>
              <MorphologicalSubrule id="subExA">
                <MorphologicalInput><PhoneticSequence id="stemExA"><OptionalSegmentSequence min="1" max="-1"><SimpleContext naturalClass="ncAny" /></OptionalSegmentSequence></PhoneticSequence></MorphologicalInput>
                <MorphologicalOutput><CopyFromInput index="stemExA" /><InsertSegments><PhoneticShape>ke</PhoneticShape></InsertSegments></MorphologicalOutput>
              </MorphologicalSubrule>
            </MorphologicalSubrules>
            <MorphemeId>EXA</MorphemeId>
            <Gloss>exa</Gloss>
          </MorphologicalRule>
          <MorphologicalRule id="mrExB" requiredPartsOfSpeech="posN" outputPartOfSpeech="posN">
            <Name>exB</Name>
            <MorphologicalSubrules>
              <MorphologicalSubrule id="subExB">
                <MorphologicalInput><PhoneticSequence id="stemExB"><OptionalSegmentSequence min="1" max="-1"><SimpleContext naturalClass="ncAny" /></OptionalSegmentSequence></PhoneticSequence></MorphologicalInput>
                <MorphologicalOutput><CopyFromInput index="stemExB" /><InsertSegments><PhoneticShape>ko</PhoneticShape></InsertSegments></MorphologicalOutput>
              </MorphologicalSubrule>
            </MorphologicalSubrules>
            <MorphemeId>EXB</MorphemeId>
            <Gloss>exb</Gloss>
          </MorphologicalRule>
          <!-- mrExC/mrExD: a SECOND isolated exclude pair, added specifically to restore
               dtd:enum/AllomorphCoOccurrenceRule/adjacency/{adjacentToLeft,adjacentToRight,
               somewhereToLeft,somewhereToRight} coverage. The mrExA/mrExB pair above only exercises
               "anywhere" (Allomorph) and "adjacentToRight" (Morpheme, a separate DTD surface); the
               other four AllomorphCoOccurrenceRule adjacency values had no other witness anywhere in
               this suite once the pre-conversion type="require" material (four different adjacency
               values, on mrCoA-D) was removed. See the AllomorphCoOccurrenceRules element below:
               ExC/ExD are always adjacent when both present (fixed Slot order, no rule between their
               two slots), so one word ("toplane") exercises all four non-default adjacency values at
               once via four separate rule declarations over the SAME underlying fact, exactly as
               mrConferExcl/mrExclReader already model a single fact two ways elsewhere in this file. -->
          <MorphologicalRule id="mrExC" requiredPartsOfSpeech="posN" outputPartOfSpeech="posN">
            <Name>exC</Name>
            <MorphologicalSubrules>
              <MorphologicalSubrule id="subExC">
                <MorphologicalInput><PhoneticSequence id="stemExC"><OptionalSegmentSequence min="1" max="-1"><SimpleContext naturalClass="ncAny" /></OptionalSegmentSequence></PhoneticSequence></MorphologicalInput>
                <MorphologicalOutput><CopyFromInput index="stemExC" /><InsertSegments><PhoneticShape>la</PhoneticShape></InsertSegments></MorphologicalOutput>
              </MorphologicalSubrule>
            </MorphologicalSubrules>
            <MorphemeId>EXC</MorphemeId>
            <Gloss>exc</Gloss>
          </MorphologicalRule>
          <MorphologicalRule id="mrExD" requiredPartsOfSpeech="posN" outputPartOfSpeech="posN">
            <Name>exD</Name>
            <MorphologicalSubrules>
              <MorphologicalSubrule id="subExD">
                <MorphologicalInput><PhoneticSequence id="stemExD"><OptionalSegmentSequence min="1" max="-1"><SimpleContext naturalClass="ncAny" /></OptionalSegmentSequence></PhoneticSequence></MorphologicalInput>
                <MorphologicalOutput><CopyFromInput index="stemExD" /><InsertSegments><PhoneticShape>ne</PhoneticShape></InsertSegments></MorphologicalOutput>
              </MorphologicalSubrule>
            </MorphologicalSubrules>
            <MorphemeId>EXD</MorphemeId>
            <Gloss>exd</Gloss>
          </MorphologicalRule>
        </MorphologicalRuleDefinitions>
        <AffixTemplates>
          <!-- The FINAL template. A stratum whose only template is non-final admits no complete word
               at all (confirmed against the C# oracle: with just the non-final template below, even a
               bare root produced zero parses), so a final template has to exist alongside it. -->
          <AffixTemplate requiredPartsOfSpeech="posN">
            <Name>finalTemplate</Name>
